  "slug": "variant-foundation-90f7",
  "summary": "Five preprints extend DNA and RNA foundation models to variant scoring, personal epigenomes, lncRNAs and fungal genomes, with benchmarks in LGMD genes.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the adaptation of pretrained sequence models to variant-level or genome-specific prediction tasks. LncRFM extends pretraining to lncRNAs (24.7M sequences) with structure-guided masking; FunDLM does so for 426 fungal genomes, scoring missense and start/stop variants. HapAdapter adds a lightweight adapter so models can infer allele-specific epigenomic effects from diploid personal genomes. A benchmark of six genomic foundation models on 6,960 ClinVar variants in LGMD genes found Evo2 with 501 bp context best, though clinical utility is untested. SpliceVarMech takes a different route, a causal generative framework with Bayesian inference to infer mechanisms of non-canonical splicing variants, evaluated on male infertility genes and BRCA1. Together they shift emphasis from raw scoring toward adaptation, context length and mechanistic interpretation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
